            "language": "markdown",
            "showLineNumbers": false,
            "showMiniMap": false
          },
          "content": "## 📋 How to Load Your Apps & Devices from Excel (Step-by-Step)\n\n**This dashboard is now fully filtered to *only* the servers in your Excel.**\n\n### 1. For Devices / Instances (Quick - No Prometheus Change Needed)\n1. Open your Excel file.\n2. Copy the column with **hostnames / instance names** (the servers for your apps).\n3. In Grafana:\n   - Go to dashboard **variables** (top bar).\n   - Click **Instance (Excel list filter)**.\n   - **Best options**:\n     - Paste a **regex** that matches your hosts, e.g. `prod-app1-.*|prod-app2-.*|uat-.*` (pipe `|` separated).\n     - Or change **Type** to **Custom**, paste hostnames **one per line**, enable \"Include All\", set All value to `.*`.\n4. The whole dashboard (all 4 tabs) instantly shows **only your Excel-listed devices**.\n\n### 2. For True App-Level Grouping (Recommended - One-Time Prometheus Change)\nYour Excel likely has an **App** column. To get perfect \"per app\" summaries in Tab 3 & Tab 4:\n1. In your **Prometheus scrape config** (or relabel_configs), add the app name as a label for these hosts. Example:\n   ```yaml\n   static_configs:\n     - targets: ['host1:9100', 'host2:9100']\n       labels:\n         app: 'PaymentService'          # from your Excel\n         env: 'prod'\n   ```\n   Or use relabeling to map from address or another label.\n2. In Grafana variables, the **App** variable will now populate automatically (or change it to Custom and paste app names from Excel).\n3. Tabs 3 & 4 will then show clean per-app RAG, trends, and breakdowns.\n\n**Why do this?** Once the `app` label is added, Tab 3 gives executive view per application, and Tab 4 shows exactly which servers belong to which app with RAG status.\n\n**Current behavior (works immediately):** Tabs 3 & 4 fall back to grouping by **Job** (device type) until you add the `app` label. Still very useful.\n\n**Tips:**\n- Use your Excel as the source of truth — update Prometheus labels when Excel changes.\n- Add more labels like `env`, `datacenter`, `owner` from Excel columns for even richer filtering.\n- The dashboard auto-refreshes every 30s. Perfect for big days!\n\n*Updated with 4 tabs + full Excel guidance. Import/replace the JSON and set the Instance (and App) variables from your Excel.*",
          "mode": "markdown"
        },
        "pluginVersion": "10.4.0",
        "title": "📖 Full Instructions: 4 Tabs + Loading from Excel",
        "type": "text"
      }
